<Base title="Support — Pegboard Seven"
      description="Answers to the things people actually write in about, and an address that a person reads."
      current="legal">

  <section>
    <p class="kicker">Pegboard Seven · Support</p>
    <h1 style="max-width:20ch">Most of it is answered here.</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="prose">

<h2>I bought coins and they did not arrive</h2>
<p>
  Open <strong>SHOP</strong> and tap <strong>RESTORE PURCHASES</strong>. Apple
  re-sends every purchase made with your Apple ID and the app applies it again.
  This is also what to use after reinstalling or moving to a new phone.
</p>
<p>
  If it still does not appear, the charge is with Apple rather than with us —
  write to us and we will help, but a refund can only come from
  <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
</p>

<h2>I lost my progress</h2>
<p>
  Progress is stored on the phone, not on a server — there is no account to log
  back into. Deleting the app deletes it, and it does not move to a new device.
  Purchases are the exception and come back with <strong>RESTORE
  PURCHASES</strong>.
</p>
<p>
  We would rather say this plainly than let you look for a login that does not
  exist.
</p>

<h2>The tray filled up and I lost</h2>
<p>
  That is the rule, not a bug: a screw whose colour the open bin is not asking
  for goes to the tray, and a full tray ends the level. The tray is your margin
  for error, not a second bin.
</p>
<p>
  When it happens you are offered a way to continue with coins — empty the tray,
  buy extra moves, or add a slot. You are never required to pay: restarting the
  level is always free.
</p>

<h2>I am stuck on a level</h2>
<p>
  Every level is solvable without ever using the tray — that is checked
  automatically before it ships, all 300 of them. If one feels impossible it is
  usually the order: take the screw that <em>unblocks</em> a plate first, rather
  than the one whose colour is open now.
</p>
<p>
  Boosters exist for the rest — undo a move, swap a colour, add a slot — and all
  of them are bought with coins you earn by playing.
</p>

<h2>How do I get coins?</h2>
<p>
  By finishing levels. Stars pay more than a bare clear, finishing a chapter for
  the first time pays a bonus, and there is a daily reward that grows over a
  week. Coins can also be bought, but nothing in the game is locked behind
  buying them.
</p>

<h2>Are there ads?</h2>
<p>
  Not in this version. No banners, no interstitials, no rewarded videos, and no
  tracking prompt.
</p>

<h2>Sound and haptics</h2>
<p>
  Both are in <strong>MORE</strong>, and both are remembered.
</p>

<h2>Nothing here matches</h2>
<p>
  Write to <a href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a>.
  A person reads it and replies within three working days. It helps to say which
  level number you were on and what your iPhone is.
</p>

<p class="fine">
  Pegboard Seven is made by Nurçin Ehlimanoğlu, a sole proprietorship in
  Türkiye. See also the
  <a href="/pegboard-seven-privacy">privacy policy</a> and the
  <a href="/pegboard-seven-terms">terms of use</a>.
</p>
